From 455ec46b57b3416f39a946766b9867b0b65e0786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:59:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix token badge 'err'; add private notepad, installer/manager

- Token badge: the request to count.php?note=... matched the EasyPrivacy
  rule '/count.php?', so ad blockers dropped it in the browser and the
  badge showed 'err'. Counts are now served from the note's own URL,
  GET /<note>?tokens=1 (index.php). count.php removed.
- Badge errors now say what failed: 'err 502', 'err net', 'err json'.
- Two notepads: public on 5555 (/data/raw_note_d) and private with HTTP
  basic auth on 7777 (/data/raw_note_d_passwd). The private one refuses
  to start without a user and password.
- Tokenizer: /count/<space>/<name>; each notepad counts only its own
  folder (NOTE_SPACE / NOTE_SPACES).
- install_manger.sh: --install (no questions) and an interactive manager
  (status, start/stop/restart, logs, update, login, ports, listen IP,
  time zone, note folders, backup, uninstall). Installs 'raw_note' command.
- search.php: snippet position used a byte offset as a character offset,
  so snippets for Chinese text were off; highlight regex now UTF-8 aware.
- list.php/search.php: '...' shown only when text is really truncated.
- Dockerfile: ServerName set (silences AH00558).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5571eWQ1xTsjV8G6DCKon
